      "message": "Solving issue #799. BoundedVector::data() is unusable.  (#978)\n\n* Solving issue #799. I believe that pointer returned by data should be of type Tp with which the class is templated with and therefore ! next to std::is_same<T, Tp>::value is typo and can be replaced with T=Tp for the method to work\n\nSigned-off-by: UseVix <jozef.franciszek.wiatr@gmail.com>\n\n* Add unit tests for BoundedVector::data() and fix code formatting\n\nSigned-off-by: William Woodall <wjwwood@google.com>\n\n* Add unit tests for BoundedVector::data() and fix code formatting\n\nSigned-off-by: William Woodall <wjwwood@google.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: UseVix <jozef.franciszek.wiatr@gmail.com>\nSigned-off-by: William Woodall <wjwwood@google.com>\nCo-authored-by: UseVix <jozef.franciszek.wiatr@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: William Woodall <wjwwood@google.com>",
